```

## Example from Class
While `SIGINT` is not in our provided notes, it is typically implemented using the `signal.h` library. You would define a function to handle the interrupt and then tell the system to use it:

```c
#include <signal.h>
#include <stdio.h>

void handle_sigint(int sig) {
    printf("\nCaught the signal! Cleaning up...\n");
}

int main() {
    signal(SIGINT, handle_sigint);
    // Program logic goes here
    return 0;
}
```

